s%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F660a1595-cde7-4cb5-aaae-094fe61627db_2612x2070.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Premiums vs. Wages, 2007-2019</figcaption></figure></div><p>And great for their CEOs: </p><div class=\"embedded-post-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;id&quot;:124887914,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://wendellpotter.substack.com/p/335-million-take-home-here-are-the&quot;,&quot;publication_id&quot;:255152,&quot;embedding_publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;HEALTH CARE un-covered&quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd32a5be-35a1-44f4-8e89-5c52fee739ab_1280x1280.png&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;$335 million take-home: here are the 7 health insurance CEOs who made it big in 2022&quot;,&quot;truncated_body_text&quot;:&quot;I wrote last month about how big health insurance companies have been on a spending spree buying back shares of their own stock, a gimmick–illegal until a few years ago–that has made a few insurance company CEOs incredibly rich at a time when 100 million Americans are saddled with medical debt&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2023-06-01T18:39:12.070Z&quot;,&quot;like_count&quot;:24,&quot;comment_count&quot;:5,&quot;bylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:20146153,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Wendell Potter&quot;,&quot;handle&quot;:&quot;wendellpotter&quot;,&quot;previous_name&quot;:&quot;Wendell Potter Now&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/695c8ca3-3b7a-48cc-96ae-407cc7a42713_1030x1030.jpeg&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Former VP, @cigna. Whistleblower and reformed insurance propagandist. President, @cforhd. Press: andrew@feldmanstrategies.com. Speeches: info@harrywalker.com.&quot;,&quot;profile_set_up_at&quot;:&quot;2021-05-24T17:39:16.511Z&quot;,&quot;publicationUsers&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:213388,&quot;user_id&quot;:20146153,&quot;publication_id&quot;:255152,&quot;role&quot;:&quot;admin&quot;,&quot;public&quot;:true,&quot;is_primary&quot;:false,&quot;publication&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:255152,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;HEALTH CARE un-covered&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;wendellpotter&quot;,&quot;custom_domain&quot;:null,&quot;custom_domain_optional&quot;:false,&quot;hero_text&quot;:&quot;Pulling back the curtains on how Big Health is hurting Americans and how we got to this point. &quot;,&quot;logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/cd32a5be-35a1-44f4-8e89-5c52fee739ab_1280x1280.png&quot;,&quot;author_id&quot;:20146153,&quot;theme_var_background_pop&quot;:&quot;#BAA049&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2021-01-05T17:29:27.102Z&quot;,&quot;rss_website_url&quot;:null,&quot;email_from_name&quot;:&quot;HEALTH CARE un-covered&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;Wendell Potter&quot;,&quot;founding_plan_name&quot;:&quot;Sustaining subscription&quot;,&quot;community_enabled&quot;:true,&quot;invite_only&quot;:false,&quot;payments_state&quot;:&quot;enabled&quot;}}],&quot;twitter_screen_name&quot;:&quot;wendellpotter&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;utm_campaign&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"EmbeddedPostToDOM\"><a class=\"embedded-post\" native=\"true\" href=\"https://wendellpotter.substack.com/p/335-million-take-home-here-are-the?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web\"><div class=\"embedded-post-header\"><img class=\"embedded-post-publication-logo\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HwPF!,w_56,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd32a5be-35a1-44f4-8e89-5c52fee739ab_1280x1280.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"embedded-post-publication-name\">HEALTH CARE un-covered</span></div><div class=\"embedded-post-title-wrapper\"><div class=\"embedded-post-title\">$335 million take-home: here are the 7 health insurance CEOs who made it big in 2022</div></div><div class=\"embedded-post-body\">I wrote last month about how big health insurance companies have been on a spending spree buying back shares of their own stock, a gimmick–illegal until a few years ago–that has made a few insurance company CEOs incredibly rich at a time when 100 million Americans are saddled with medical debt…</div><div class=\"embedded-post-cta-wrapper\"><span class=\"embedded-post-cta\">Read more</span></div><div class=\"embedded-post-meta\">3 years ago · 24 likes · 5 comments · Wendell Potter</div></a></div><p>For consumers paying premiums, it is less of a stellar arrangement; they are going up!</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png\" width=\"550\" height=\"341.1057692307692\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/af4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:903,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:550,&quot;bytes&quot;:183049,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JPta!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Faf4e873e-ba09-4be3-9309-3dc261ba8bd0_1838x1140.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Premiums vs. Inflation, 1996-2020</figcaption></figure></div><p>For a long time, brokers could legally accept payments and didn’t have to disclose them to employers. This makes for a very cozy golf game. You want someone to have a fiduciary role because there are known penalties if they scam you. It’s not hard to compare the very, very different gross margins across plan types to see profits are not evenly distributed:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png\" width=\"526\" height=\"295.1524725274725\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/ad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:817,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:526,&quot;bytes&quot;:104678,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1NKR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad4daa16-6f23-4bcf-b4ba-8f42154f1292_3209x1800.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Gross Margins on Different Health Plans, 2018-2020</figcaption></figure></div><p>It wasn’t, technically speaking, legal to scam employers; enforcement was absent, however. Taking undisclosed payments is not even legal when it comes to getting songs played on the radio. Except it was, sort of, in healthcare.</p><p>So in 2021, it was made entirely, obviously, officially illegal for employers, and the brokers they buy insurance from, to engage in non-fiduciary behavior. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png\" width=\"512\" height=\"439.8747826086956\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:988,&quot;width&quot;:1150,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:512,&quot;bytes&quot;:57980,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Deductibles on the Rise, 2010-2018&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Deductibles on the Rise, 2010-2018\" title=\"Deductibles on the Rise, 2010-2018\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jh6s!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4a7a3275-6c3d-46eb-bf53-0154c5cd6df8_1150x988.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Deductibles on the Rise, 2010-2018</figcaption></figure></div><p>The duty, it should be noted, is to the plan member. A.k.a., the person who has the insurance coverage. A.k.a., almost all of us, from our jobs.</p><p>This has a practical upshot for every single one of us who has employer-provided health insurance under ERISA.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-4\" href=\"#footnote-4\" target=\"_self\">4</a></p><h2>We have a right for that coverage to be in our best interest. </h2><p>That has some precise definitions. Some of them are highly actionable by individuals without having to be legal scholars.</p><h3>Obvious things you can win a fight about:</h3><p>Under the accountable care act, there are rules about network sufficiency. This means all insurance by private employers covered under ERISA must meet minimum standards.</p><p>The most obvious minimum? It is the time it takes to get an appointment.</p><p><strong>And the maximum waiting time for a mental health appointment… is…up to…</strong></p><h1><strong>Ten days.</strong></h1><p>For any outpatient appointment. For any condition.</p><p>So let’s use an undeniable and easy-to-prove example: let’s say you live in the state of Texas, Florida, Utah, Arkansas, etc. </p><p>Let’s say you have a child with gender dysphoria. </p><p>In states with bans on gender-affirming care, the wait time for an appointment for your child’s gender dysphoria, assessment, or treatment, is now <em>infinite</em><a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-5\" href=\"#footnote-5\" target=\"_self\">5</a>.  </p><p>Now let us imagine you’re looking for transcranial magnetic stimulation for your treatment-resistant obsessive-compulsive disorder. Imagine you have health insurance other than one run by the <a href=\"https://www.cigna.com/knowledge-center/hw/medical-topics/transcranial-magnetic-stimulation-acm0577\">wise administrators at Evernorth</a>  (a.k.a. CIGNA).</p><p>There is only one FDA-cleared treatment for treatment-resistant obsessive-compulsive disorder. It’s TMS (<a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-permits-marketing-transcranial-magnetic-stimulation-treatment-obsessive-compulsive-disorder\">Ideally with the Brainsway H7 coil</a>). If you have almost all Big  Payer plans, you have an employer that has purchased health insurance <em>that never pays</em> for the treatment—<a href=\"https://public.providerexpress.com/content/dam/ope-provexpr/us/pdfs/clinResourcesMain/guidelines/bcp/tmsMCS.pdf\">it’s a plan exclusion!</a></p><p>That is, conceivably, a breach of fiduciary duty to you— because you have a right to mental health parity in your health insurance. If there’s an FDA-approved treatment that your insurance will never cover, you have the right to sue your employer for buying insurance that doesn’t cover the thing. It’s an open question if subsequent legal action can also <a href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/the-ada-compliant-end-of-life-quality\">recoup damages related to delays in treatment.</a></p><h2>The Covering Of @&amp;$ Begins.</h2><p>Your employer needs to get compliant. And they’re probably going to call their Benefits Broker. It is in the interests of those parties to file suit to cover their own liability, too.</p><p>At a bare minimum, they’re probably going to want to buy a compliant plan during the next enrollment cycle. Who the heck would want to stand in the way of that <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj7lvOk89z_AhVKEVkFHdglAR4QFnoECBUQAQ&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.freep.com%2Fstory%2Fmoney%2Fcars%2Fford%2F2023%2F06%2F01%2Fford-sues-blue-cross-alleged-price-fixing%2F70279180007%2F&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MS8VNbLlbp2tEeGU7LF5F&amp;opi=89978449\">particular wrecking ball?</a> Or go to a self-funded plan where they can make sure they're compliant using a tool like the <a href=\"http://members.healthrosetta.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Plan-Grader-Sell-Sheet-Flier.pdf\">Health Rosetta Plan Grader.</a></p><p>Now, those are obvious cases. If you think your benefits suck, from a regulatory standpoint, that’s probably true.</p><p>And if ERISA wasn’t bad enough,<a href=\"https://www.oyez.org/cases/2022/21-887\"> I suspect Perez v. Sturgis</a> will be applied for damages under ADA next. <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/have-health-benefits-become-a-huge?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Health Plans— the new Lawyer Employment Act of 2023!</a></p><p>I was planning to offer my readers the opportunity to buckle up. On compliance audit, it looks like we're all out of buckles, given the number of regulatory updates recently!</p><p>You can still…</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p></p><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>I have seven-year-old children who enjoy this kind of humor.</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">2</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Depending on the size of your employer, blah blah blah. This stuff is boring. Let’s not pretend otherwise.  </p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-3\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-3\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">3</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>It doesn’t apply to people who work for the government.</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-4\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-4\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">4</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p> this excludes government employees and some other groups.</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-5\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-5\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">5</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Or, at the very least, until Governor Gregory Abbott is run out of town on a rail. Because when he defined gender-affirming care as child abuse, he assured that people would not put themselves at risk of documenting accurately, and so there probably are no available gender-affirming care visits in the state of Texas. And, whether you like it or not, that’s a condition listed in the DSM 5. So it falls under a behavioral health appointment according to the ACA, and your health plan is legally only allowed to make you wait ten days for an appointment.</p><p></p></div></div>","text":"The Frontier Psychiatrists is a daily health-related newsletter. It has a humorous tone about serious issues. Owen Muir, M.D., writes most of it. Today—because it’s a lazy Saturday—we feature light reading about health insurance and compliance standards under ERISA!\n\nGuess what? Chicken butt. Guess why? Because there’s a regulatory compliance enforcement opportunity or disaster, depending on your perspective. Also, chicken thigh. 1\n\nDo you know health insurance comes out of your paycheck before taxes? If you do have a job and it offers health benefits, you have the option of health insurance. 2\n\nIt turns out that for employer-provided health insurance in the U.S. if your employer has to comply with ERISA 3 , they have significant liability. As of 2021, Fiduciary Duty was definitively added to the Combined Appropriations Act.\n\nYour Author Looks for Oranges In the Literal Hardware Store.\n\nWhat’s a fiduciary? A fiduciary is someone who has to act in your best interest. This is defined financially. Your benefits can’t provide coverage below minimum legal standards when paying for health benefits. The audit standards are laid out by the Department of Labor, which is helpfully accessible here.\n\nShare The Frontier Psychiatrists\n\nCompliance with these laws is what makes health insurance pre-tax. It’s employment law. It’s tax law. It’s both. It’s the Pizza Hut and Taco Bell of legal statutes in the same convenient place!\n\nThe health insurance business is good to be in…for payers:\n\nPremiums vs. Wages, 2007-2019\n\nAnd great for their CEOs:\n\nHEALTH CARE un-covered\n\n$335 million take-home: here are the 7 health insurance CEOs who made it big in 2022\n\nI wrote last month about how big health insurance companies have been on a spending spree buying back shares of their own stock, a gimmick–illegal until a few years ago–that has made a few insurance company CEOs incredibly rich at a time when 100 million Americans are saddled with medical debt…\n\nRead more\n\n3 years ago · 24 likes · 5 comments · Wendell Potter\n\nFor consumers paying premiums, it is less of a stellar arrangement; they are going up!\n\nPremiums vs. Inflation, 1996-2020\n\nFor a long time, brokers could legally accept payments and didn’t have to disclose them to employers. This makes for a very cozy golf game. You want someone to have a fiduciary role because there are known penalties if they scam you. It’s not hard to compare the very, very different gross margins across plan types to see profits are not evenly distributed:\n\nGross Margins on Different Health Plans, 2018-2020\n\nIt wasn’t, technically speaking, legal to scam employers; enforcement was absent, however. Taking undisclosed payments is not even legal when it comes to getting songs played on the radio. Except it was, sort of, in healthcare.\n\nSo in 2021, it was made entirely, obviously, officially illegal for employers, and the brokers they buy insurance from, to engage in non-fiduciary behavior.\n\nDeductibles on the Rise, 2010-2018\n\nThe duty, it should be noted, is to the plan member. A.k.a., the person who has the insurance coverage. A.k.a., almost all of us, from our jobs.\n\nThis has a practical upshot for every single one of us who has employer-provided health insurance under ERISA. 4\n\nWe have a right for that coverage to be in our best interest.\n\nThat has some precise definitions. Some of them are highly actionable by individuals without having to be legal scholars.\n\nObvious things you can win a fight about:\n\nUnder the accountable care act, there are rules about network sufficiency. This means all insurance by private employers covered under ERISA must meet minimum standards.\n\nThe most obvious minimum? It is the time it takes to get an appointment.\n\nAnd the maximum waiting time for a mental health appointment… is…up to…\n\nTen days.\n\nFor any outpatient appointment. For any condition.\n\nSo let’s use an undeniable and easy-to-prove example: let’s say you live in the state of Texas, Florida, Utah, Arkansas, etc.\n\nLet’s say you have a child with gender dysphoria.\n\nIn states with bans on gender-affirming care, the wait time for an appointment for your child’s gender dysphoria, assessment, or treatment, is now infinite 5 .\n\nNow let us imagine you’re looking for transcranial magnetic stimulation for your treatment-resistant obsessive-compulsive disorder. Imagine you have health insurance other than one run by the wise administrators at Evernorth (a.k.a. CIGNA).\n\nThere is only one FDA-cleared treatment for treatment-resistant obsessive-compulsive disorder. It’s TMS ( Ideally with the Brainsway H7 coil ). If you have almost all Big Payer plans, you have an employer that has purchased health insurance that never pays for the treatment— it’s a plan exclusion!\n\nThat is, conceivably, a breach of fiduciary duty to you— because you have a right to mental health parity in your health insurance. If there’s an FDA-approved treatment that your insurance will never cover, you have the right to sue your employer for buying insurance that doesn’t cover the thing. It’s an open question if subsequent legal action can also recoup damages related to delays in treatment.\n\nThe Covering Of @&$ Begins.\n\nYour employer needs to get compliant. And they’re probably going to call their Benefits Broker. It is in the interests of those parties to file suit to cover their own liability, too.\n\nAt a bare minimum, they’re probably going to want to buy a compliant plan during the next enrollment cycle. Who the heck would want to stand in the way of that particular wrecking ball? Or go to a self-funded plan where they can make sure they're compliant using a tool like the Health Rosetta Plan Grader.\n\nNow, those are obvious cases. If you think your benefits suck, from a regulatory standpoint, that’s probably true.\n\nAnd if ERISA wasn’t bad enough, I suspect Perez v. Sturgis will be applied for damages under ADA next. Health Plans— the new Lawyer Employment Act of 2023!\n\nI was planning to offer my readers the opportunity to buckle up. On compliance audit, it looks like we're all out of buckles, given the number of regulatory updates recently!\n\nYou can still…\n\nSubscribe now\n\n1 I have seven-year-old children who enjoy this kind of humor.\n\n2 Depending on the size of your employer, blah blah blah. This stuff is boring. Let’s not pretend otherwise.\n\n3 It doesn’t apply to people who work for the government.\n\n4 this excludes government employees and some other groups.\n\n5 Or, at the very least, until Governor Gregory Abbott is run out of town on a rail. Because when he defined gender-affirming care as child abuse, he assured that people would not put themselves at risk of documenting accurately, and so there probably are no available gender-affirming care visits in the state of Texas. And, whether you like it or not, that’s a condition listed in the DSM 5. So it falls under a behavioral health appointment according to the ACA, and your health plan is legally only allowed to make you wait ten days for an appointment."}